# State management

Pick one tool per job. Do not introduce Riverpod, Provider, or GetX controllers.

| Job | Tool | Rebuild |
|---|---|---|
| Page-local value (tab, counter, form flag) | `ObsValue<T>` on the page `Controller` | `ObsValueConsumer` |
| Async fetch (API / fake repo) | `Requester<T>` in `domain/requesters/` | `RequesterConsumer` |
| Shared session / device | `Cubit` via `BlocProvider` (`DeviceCubit`, `AuthCubit`) | `BlocBuilder` |
| Generic load/success/fail | `BaseBloc<T>` | `BaseBlocBuilder` |

```dart
// Controller
final ObsValue<int> tabObs = ObsValue.withInit(0);
void onTab(int i) => tabObs.setValue(i);

// UI
ObsValueConsumer(
  observable: controller.tabObs,
  builder: (context, index) => AppSegmented(items: const ['إيجار', 'شراء'], index: index, onChanged: controller.onTab),
)
```

```dart
// Requester
class HomeRequester extends Requester<List<Listing>> {
  @override
  Future<void> request({bool fromRemote = true}) async {
    loadingState();
    final result = await getIt<HomeRepository>().getFeed();
    result.when(isSuccess: successState, isError: (e) => failedState(e, request));
  }
}
```

Do not call `setState` for business data. Do not put UI widgets inside the controller. Do not keep `BuildContext` as a field.
